# The ledger of `kafka`: what a program does with a Kafka cluster, measured
# against Go's github.com/segmentio/kafka-go v0.4.51 and
# github.com/twmb/franz-go v1.22.3 (`kgo`, and `kerr` for the errors; their
# `go doc -all`, fetched into the scratch folder on 2026-11-18), Python's
# kafka-python 3.0.13 and confluent-kafka 2.16.2 (`dir` of their producers,
# consumers, admin clients and messages, installed into the scratch folder
# the same day), and Rust's rdkafka 0.39.0 (its docs.rs items, read the same
# day).
#
# The layout of each request and answer was read from the message
# definitions Apache Kafka publishes, which kafka-python carries as JSON, at
# the version this client speaks: ApiVersions 2, Metadata 8, Produce 8, Fetch
# 11, ListOffsets 5, FindCoordinator 2, OffsetCommit 7, OffsetFetch 5,
# JoinGroup 5, SyncGroup 3, Heartbeat 3, LeaveGroup 3, SaslHandshake 1,
# SaslAuthenticate 1, CreateTopics 4, DeleteTopics 3, CreatePartitions 1,
# DeleteRecords 1, ListGroups 2, DescribeGroups 4, DeleteGroups 1: the
# newest of each that is not flexible, all of them read by Kafka 2.4 to 4.x.
# The expected values of the tests were asked of kafka-python (a record
# batch's bytes, a gzip batch, a transactional batch, MurmurHash2's
# partitions, the range assignor, a subscription's bytes), of confluent-kafka
# (MurmurHash2's partitions), of franz-go's `kerr` (the errors' names) and of
# RFC 7677 (SCRAM-SHA-256's example). The live run, on 2026-11-18, reached
# Apache Kafka 4.1.1 (the image apache/kafka:4.1.1, KRaft, one node) in a
# container of this Mac: plain, SASL PLAIN, SCRAM-SHA-256 and SCRAM-SHA-512,
# and TLS.

capability kafka/connect  a client of a cluster: the first broker that answers, its versions asked, the cluster's brokers learned
  heroes  kafka.connect, kafka.options, kafka.Options, kafka.Client, kafka.close, kafka.is_closed, kafka.DEFAULT_PORT
  go      Dial, DialContext, Dialer, Dialer.Dial, Dialer.DialContext, NewConn, NewConnWith, Conn, ConnConfig, Conn.Close, Client, Transport, Transport.CloseIdleConnections, kgo.NewClient, kgo.SeedBrokers, kgo.ClientID, kgo.DialTimeout, kgo.RequestRetries, kgo.RetryTimeout, kgo.Client.Close, kgo.Client.SeedBrokers, kgo.Client.UpdateSeedBrokers, kgo.Client.Ping, kgo.Client.DiscoveredBrokers, kgo.Client.Broker
  rust    config::ClientConfig, client::Client, config::FromClientConfig
  python  KafkaProducer, KafkaConsumer, KafkaAdminClient, KafkaProducer.close, KafkaConsumer.close, KafkaAdminClient.close, KafkaProducer.bootstrap_connected, KafkaConsumer.bootstrap_connected, confluent_kafka.Producer, confluent_kafka.Consumer, confluent_kafka.admin.AdminClient
  note    one client for producing, fetching and the cluster's administration, as kafka-go's Client and franz-go's kgo.Client are; a consumer of a group is its own value, `subscribe`'s

capability kafka/tls  TLS on every connection, the broker's certificate checked
  heroes  kafka.Options (tls, roots)
  go      Dialer.TLS, kgo.DialTLS, kgo.DialTLSConfig
  rust    ClientConfig (security.protocol ssl)
  python  KafkaProducer(security_protocol, ssl_cafile), confluent_kafka (security.protocol)
  note    a client certificate is not presented, which `tls` does not offer

capability kafka/sasl  SASL PLAIN, SCRAM-SHA-256 and SCRAM-SHA-512, over TLS or not
  heroes  kafka.Options (sasl), kafka.Sasl
  go      Dialer.SASLMechanism, ScramMechanism, sasl/plain.Mechanism, sasl/scram.Mechanism, sasl/scram.SHA256, sasl/scram.SHA512, kgo.SASL
  rust    ClientConfig (sasl.mechanism, sasl.username, sasl.password)
  python  KafkaProducer(sasl_mechanism, sasl_plain_username, sasl_plain_password), confluent_kafka.Producer.set_sasl_credentials, confluent_kafka.Consumer.set_sasl_credentials, confluent_kafka.admin.AdminClient.set_sasl_credentials
  note    the server's SCRAM signature is checked, so a server that does not know the password cannot pass for one that does

capability kafka/sasl-other  SASL GSSAPI (Kerberos), OAUTHBEARER, AWS's MSK IAM
  heroes  pending: OAUTHBEARER is one message carrying a token, which waits for a variant of `Sasl` and its refresh; GSSAPI needs the system's Kerberos library, which no package of Rebel binds; MSK IAM signs with AWS's Signature Version 4, `s3`'s, above this package's layer
  go      -
  rust    client::OAuthToken
  python  KafkaProducer(sasl_mechanism="GSSAPI" or "OAUTHBEARER"), confluent_kafka (sasl.oauthbearer.*)

capability kafka/api-versions  the versions each request a broker reads, and this client's checked against them
  heroes  kafka.api_versions_of, kafka.ApiVersion
  go      ApiVersion, ApiVersion.Format, Conn.ApiVersions, Client.ApiVersions, Version, Version.Marshal, Version.Unmarshal, kgo.MaxVersions, kgo.MinVersions
  rust    types::RDKafkaApiKey
  python  KafkaAdminClient.api_versions, KafkaAdminClient.get_broker_version_data
  note    a broker that does not read the version this client speaks is `unsupported`, naming its range

