capability kafka/produce  messages written to one partition in one batch, the leader's answer read
  heroes  kafka.produce, kafka.Produced
  go      Conn.WriteMessages, Conn.WriteCompressedMessages, Conn.WriteCompressedMessagesAt, Conn.Write, Conn.SetRequiredAcks, DialLeader, Dialer.DialLeader, Client.Produce, Client.RawProduce, kgo.Client.ProduceSync, kgo.ProduceResult, kgo.ProduceResults, kgo.ProduceResults.First, kgo.ProduceResults.FirstErr
  rust    producer::BaseProducer, producer::BaseRecord, producer::Producer
  python  -
  note    a leader moved or not ready is retried within `Options.wait_ms`; without idempotence a batch whose answer was lost may be written twice

capability kafka/send  messages written to their topics and partitions, a batch for each partition and a request for each leader, their offsets answered
  heroes  kafka.send, kafka.message, kafka.with_key, kafka.with_header, kafka.Message
  go      Writer, NewWriter, WriterConfig, WriterConfig.Validate, Writer.WriteMessages, Writer.Close, Message, WriteErrors, WriteErrors.Count, WriteErrors.Error, MessageTooLargeError, kgo.Client.Produce, kgo.Client.TryProduce, kgo.Record, kgo.KeySliceRecord, kgo.KeyStringRecord, kgo.SliceRecord, kgo.StringRecord, kgo.DefaultProduceTopic, kgo.DefaultProduceTopicAlways, kgo.ProducerBatchMaxBytes, kgo.ProduceRequestTimeout, kgo.RecordRetries, kgo.RecordDeliveryTimeout, kgo.UnknownTopicRetries
  rust    producer::FutureProducer, producer::FutureRecord, producer::ThreadedProducer, producer::future_producer::Delivery, producer::DeliveryFuture, producer::DeliveryResult
  python  KafkaProducer.send, confluent_kafka.Producer.produce, confluent_kafka.Producer.produce_batch, confluent_kafka.Message
  note    a call writes what it is given and answers when every partition answered, so batching is the program's list; Go's Writer and Python's send batch in the background

capability kafka/linger  a producer that buffers messages and writes them in the background after a linger
  heroes  refused: a write in the background needs a thread the program does not own, and its failure would come back to no call; the program collects its messages and calls `send` once
  go      WriterConfig (BatchSize, BatchBytes, BatchTimeout, Async), kgo.ProducerLinger, kgo.ManualFlushing, kgo.MaxBufferedRecords, kgo.MaxBufferedBytes, kgo.MaxProduceRequestsInflightPerBroker, kgo.Client.Flush, kgo.Client.BufferedProduceRecords, kgo.Client.BufferedProduceBytes, kgo.Client.AbortBufferedRecords, kgo.Client.UnsafeAbortBufferedRecords, kgo.Client.EnsureProduceConnectionIsOpen
  rust    producer::Producer::flush, producer::Producer::purge, producer::PurgeConfig
  python  KafkaProducer.flush, confluent_kafka.Producer.flush, confluent_kafka.Producer.poll, confluent_kafka.Producer.purge

capability kafka/partitioner  the partition a message goes to: by its key as Java's client hashes it, one after another without a key, or the program's own
  heroes  kafka.partition_of, kafka.send
  go      Murmur2Balancer, Murmur2Balancer.Balance, RoundRobin, RoundRobin.Balance, Balancer, BalancerFunc, BalancerFunc.Balance, kgo.StickyKeyPartitioner, kgo.KafkaHasher, kgo.RoundRobinPartitioner, kgo.ManualPartitioner, kgo.RecordPartitioner, kgo.Partitioner, kgo.TopicPartitioner, kgo.PartitionerHasher
  rust    producer::Partitioner, producer::NoCustomPartitioner, producer::PARTITION_UA
  python  kafka.partitioner (DefaultPartitioner, murmur2), confluent_kafka.murmur2
  note    a keyed message goes where Java's client puts it, MurmurHash2 with its sign bit cleared; a keyless one goes one partition after another per topic, as kafka-go's RoundRobin does, where Java's client sticks to one per batch

