capability kafka/compression-other  batches compressed by Snappy, LZ4 or Zstandard
  heroes  pending: Kafka's Snappy is xerial's framing, for which Rebel has no codec; LZ4 and Zstandard have packages of their own, `compress/lz4` and `compress/zstd`, not yet wired here; a batch so compressed is read `unsupported`
  go      compress/snappy, compress/lz4, compress/zstd, kgo.SnappyCompression, kgo.Lz4Compression, kgo.ZstdCompression, kgo.Compressor, kgo.DefaultCompressor, kgo.Decompressor, kgo.DefaultDecompressor, kgo.WithCompressor, kgo.WithDecompressor, kgo.StreamingCompression
  rust    ClientConfig (compression.type)
  python  KafkaProducer(compression_type="snappy", "lz4" or "zstd")

capability kafka/idempotence  an idempotent producer: retries the broker deduplicates by the producer's identity and each batch's sequence
  heroes  pending: InitProducerId, the producer's epoch and a sequence per partition kept across retries and reconnections, with the broker's errors of sequence answered, wait for their own work; without them a retried batch may be written twice
  go      InitProducerID, ProducerSession, kgo.DisableIdempotentWrite, kgo.AllowIdempotentProduceCancellation, kgo.Client.ProducerID, kgo.ProducerOnDataLossDetected, kgo.StopProducerOnDataLossDetected, kgo.ErrDataLoss
  rust    ClientConfig (enable.idempotence)
  python  KafkaProducer(enable_idempotence)

