capability kafka/consumer-group  a consumer in a group: joined, assigned by the range assignor, its heartbeat and commits sent as they fall due, joined again where the group changes, left at the end
  heroes  kafka.subscribe, kafka.poll, kafka.commit, kafka.close_consumer, kafka.group_options, kafka.GroupOptions, kafka.Consumer, kafka.Start
  go      ConsumerGroup, NewConsumerGroup, ConsumerGroupConfig, ConsumerGroupConfig.Validate, ConsumerGroup.Next, ConsumerGroup.Close, Generation, Generation.Start, Generation.CommitOffsets, Reader, NewReader, ReaderConfig, ReaderConfig.Validate, Reader.ReadMessage, Reader.FetchMessage, Reader.CommitMessages, Reader.Close, Reader.Config, Client.JoinGroup, Client.SyncGroup, Client.Heartbeat, Client.LeaveGroup, GroupMember, GroupMemberAssignments, GroupMemberTopic, GroupProtocol, GroupProtocolAssignment, GroupProtocolSubscription, PartitionAssignment, kgo.ConsumerGroup, kgo.ConsumeTopics, kgo.Client.PollFetches, kgo.Client.PollRecords, kgo.Client.CommitRecords, kgo.Client.CommitUncommittedOffsets, kgo.Client.CommitMarkedOffsets, kgo.Client.MarkCommitRecords, kgo.Client.MarkCommitOffsets, kgo.Client.MarkedOffsets, kgo.Client.UncommittedOffsets, kgo.Client.LeaveGroup, kgo.Client.LeaveGroupContext, kgo.Client.GroupMetadata, kgo.Client.GetConsumeTopics, kgo.Client.AddConsumeTopics, kgo.SessionTimeout, kgo.RebalanceTimeout, kgo.HeartbeatInterval, kgo.AutoCommitInterval, kgo.DisableAutoCommit, kgo.AutoCommitMarks, kgo.GreedyAutoCommit, kgo.ConsumeResetOffset, kgo.ConsumeStartOffset, kgo.NoResetOffset, kgo.InstanceID, kgo.GroupProtocol, kgo.RequireStableFetchOffsets, kgo.ParseConsumerSyncAssignment, kgo.ErrGroupSession
  rust    consumer::StreamConsumer, consumer::BaseConsumer, consumer::Consumer::subscribe, consumer::Consumer::unsubscribe, consumer::Consumer::subscription, consumer::Consumer::poll, consumer::Consumer::commit_consumer_state, consumer::Consumer::store_offset, consumer::Consumer::group_metadata, consumer::MessageStream
  python  KafkaConsumer.subscribe, KafkaConsumer.subscription, KafkaConsumer.unsubscribe, KafkaConsumer.poll, KafkaConsumer.commit, KafkaConsumer.commit_async, KafkaConsumer.group_metadata, ConsumerGroupMetadata, confluent_kafka.Consumer.subscribe, confluent_kafka.Consumer.unsubscribe, confluent_kafka.Consumer.poll, confluent_kafka.Consumer.consume, confluent_kafka.Consumer.commit, confluent_kafka.Consumer.store_offsets, confluent_kafka.Consumer.close, confluent_kafka.Consumer.memberid, confluent_kafka.Consumer.consumer_group_metadata
  note    the heartbeat goes while `poll` runs, the program's own loop being the only one: a program that does not poll within the session's time leaves the group; the commit is `poll`'s every `auto_commit_ms`, or the program's own `commit`, at least once and never at most once

