capability kafka/position  a consumer's partitions, its position in each moved and read, its place in its group
  heroes  kafka.seek, kafka.position_of, kafka.assignment_of, kafka.member_of, kafka.TopicPartition, kafka.Member
  go      Reader.SetOffset, Reader.SetOffsetAt, Reader.Offset, Reader.Lag, Reader.ReadLag, kgo.Client.SetOffsets, kgo.Offset, kgo.Offset.At, kgo.Offset.Relative, kgo.Offset.WithEpoch, kgo.Offset.AtCommitted, kgo.EpochOffset, kgo.EpochOffset.Less, kgo.RewindOffset, kgo.LookbackOffset
  rust    consumer::Consumer::seek, consumer::Consumer::seek_partitions, consumer::Consumer::position, consumer::Consumer::assignment
  python  KafkaConsumer.seek, KafkaConsumer.seek_to_beginning, KafkaConsumer.seek_to_end, KafkaConsumer.position, KafkaConsumer.assignment, confluent_kafka.Consumer.seek, confluent_kafka.Consumer.position, confluent_kafka.Consumer.assignment
  note    a consumer's lag is `fetch`'s high watermark less `position_of`; to the start or the end is `seek` to `list_offset`'s answer

